/cost now prices mistral-small-latest at $0.15 in, $0.015 cached, $0.60 out, the current models.dev price. Before this it billed at the older mistral-small-2506 rate ($0.10 / $0.30). Build, clippy, fmt and the full cargo test all pass, and it's committed as a6e28da7 (Part of #1012).

What changed
• Mistral: src/format/cost.rs gets a new arm that matches mistral-small-latest and mistral-small-2603 by exact name. It sits before the old catch-all mistral-small arm. 2603 was in the same drift row before the change, at the same models.dev price as latest, so I named it in advance as the second id this arm would fix. mistral-small-2506 still matches models.dev at $0.10 / $0.30 and keeps that price.
• Gemini (step 3): there was room under the line cap, so gemini-2.5-flash-image (output $30/MTok) and gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts ($0.50 in / $10 out) now have exact-match arms too. Before, the plain gemini-2.5-flash arm caught both and billed them at $0.30 / $2.50.
• Size: cost.rs is at 3597 lines against the 3605 cap.

Price audit against models.dev

| | matched | drifted |
|---|---|---|
| Before | 39 | 62 |
| After | 43 | 58 |

The other fields (114 compared, 13 differing only in cache-read price, 60 unpriced, 174 catalogue rows) didn't change, so models.dev didn't move during the work. The drift count fell by exactly the four ids I named before the run, and nothing newly drifted.

Tests
• A new test in price_audit_tests.rs checks all four prices through price_of, the same lookup /cost uses. It also checks that mistral-small-2506 and plain gemini-2.5-flash keep their old prices.
• Positive control, run as one mutate→test→restore command: with the old price put back in the new arm, the test failed by name. With the price restored, it passed.
• Two existing tests asserted the outdated -latest price:
  • The previous slice's check said -latest would stay at the old price until this slice, so I removed it.
  • test_estimate_cost_mistral_small still asserts the $0.10 / $0.30 price, now on mistral-small-2506, which really is that price.

Docs and tracker
• docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md now has two Mistral Small rows (latest/2603 and other ids) and rows for Gemini Flash Image and TTS.
• I commented on #1012 with the before/after numbers, the sha, and next candidates. 58 drifted rows remain, the next ones being the zai-glm rows sharing one price and the Gemini 3.x Flash family. The next slice has only 8 lines of room in cost.rs, so its tests should go in price_audit_tests.rs.
